OpenEdge example problems

Each sub-directory contains a test case you can run with OpenEdge.
Each problem has an input script (in.*) and most include analysis
or plotting scripts (Python). Some directories contain a README.md
with additional details.

Some tests require large data files (plasma.h5, bfield.h5, .equ,
.stl geometry) that are not stored in git. Download them first:

  cd /path/to/OpenEdge
  ./download_data.sh              # all datasets
  ./download_data.sh test_gca     # single test

Test cases:

test_coulomb = Coulomb collision validation (Nanbu-Takizuka, fix coulomb/background)
test_diii_d_neutrals = plasma-neutral interaction benchmark on DIII-D axisymmetric geometry
test_droplet = droplet emission, transport, and surface-interaction workflows
test_efield_polarization = polarization-drift validation for Boris pusher
test_gravity = 3D gravity-driven ballistic transport (fix gravity validation)
test_iead = ion energy-angle distribution validation (sheath kick + spatial)
test_ionization_recombination = ionization, recombination, and charge exchange with ADAS rates
test_neutral_slab = 1-D neutral transport channel isolation tests
test_west_axi = WEST tokamak axisymmetric impurity transport validation

To run a test case:

cd /path/to/OpenEdge
./download_data.sh test_gca      # if data not yet downloaded
cd examples/test_gca
mpirun -np 4 /path/to/spa_mpi -in in.input
